class:: MidSideRatio
summary:: Mid to side energy ratio in decibels
categories:: UGens>Analysis
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/Amplitude

description::
With M=(L+R)/2 and S=(L-R)/2, computes 10*log10((sum(M.squared)+1e-24)/(sum(S.squared)+1e-24)), limited to +/-120 dB. Positive values favor centre content and negative values favor side content.

Uses an exact rolling sample window, with output held at zero until it is full. The update cost is linear in the input block size, with a once-per-window sum rebase to bound roundoff drift. Memory is two windows of doubles, allocated at initialization. Formulas are independently implemented from energy, M/S decomposition, and Pearson correlation. Silence returns zero.

Vanilla Amplitude can track channel levels separately; this UGen directly relates the channels over a fixed shared interval.

classmethods::
method:: kr

argument:: left
Left audio-rate input.

argument:: right
Right audio-rate input.

argument:: windowTime
Initialization-time rolling window, 0.001..2 seconds; default 0.05.

returns::
Mid/side ratio in dB; silence returns zero.

examples::
The source pans slowly and its right analysis channel is delayed. The measured stereo relationship sets a quiet comparison-tone pitch.
code::
(
Routine({
    ~mir2Buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
    s.sync;
    ~mir2Example = {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, ~mir2Buffer, BufRateScale.kr(~mir2Buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
        var pan = SinOsc.kr(0.15);
        var stereo = Pan2.ar(source, pan);
        var value = MidSideRatio.kr(stereo[0], DelayC.ar(stereo[1], 0.01, 0.002));
        var control = value.linlin(-18, 18, 0, 1).clip(0, 1);
        var tone = Pan2.ar(SinOsc.ar(control.linexp(0, 1, 200, 1000), 0, 0.035), pan.neg);
        (stereo * 0.2 + tone) * Line.kr(0, 1, 0.1)
    }.play;
}).play(AppClock);
)
::
Stop and release the buffer:
code::
(
~mir2Example.free;
~mir2Buffer.free;
)
::

